# Applies to every Dockerfile in infra/docker/ — all three use the repo
# root as build context (see infra/README.md for why), so this file is
# what keeps node_modules, venvs, and local caches out of every image's
# build context and layers.

.git/
.github/

**/node_modules/
**/.next/
# Same reason as the .venv paths below: the glob above is not applied
# early enough to stop the context walker descending into a build output
# full of symlinks, and a Next standalone bundle contains node_modules
# links (argon2) that Docker Desktop on Windows cannot open.
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/node_modules/
**/.turbo/
**/dist/

**/.venv/
# Listed explicitly as well as by the glob above. A uv-created venv
# contains a `lib64 -> lib` symlink; when the venv was created from WSL
# and the build runs through Docker Desktop on Windows, the context
# walker fails on that link with "the file cannot be accessed by the
# system" *before* the glob is applied. The explicit paths are matched
# earlier and skip the directory outright.
apps/api/.venv/
apps/worker/.venv/
packages/python-shared/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

**/*.log
.DS_Store

.claude/
docs/
*.md
!apps/**/*.md

.vscode/
